    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d545">

                <pb facs="0764" n="684" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg684"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.4131/183: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-09-09T18:00:00+01:00">September 9,
                            1936—6 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 9—1:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>425. Your 324, September 3, 6 p.m., and 327, September 4, 6 p.m.<anchor n="45"
                        xml:id="d545-f1"/> Eden is ill and confined to his house. I shall, however,
                    make every endeavor to see him as soon as he returns to the Foreign Office and
                    before he leaves for Geneva. I have no suggestions to offer for change in the
                    text of your memorandum.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bingham</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d545-f1" n="45" xml:id="d545-f1-content">
                <p>Latter not printed; it concerned the U. S. representations regarding the
                    Anglo-Peruvian Commercial Agreement (see <ref target="frus1936v05#pg_908">vol.
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">v</hi>, pp. 908</ref> ff.).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
